Add SpaceRegistry, the per-profile list of spaces.

A Space is a named, colored set of tabs. SpaceRegistry keeps the profile's
spaces in the helium_spaces.spaces list pref, always with exactly one
permanent default space. No UI yet; nothing reads it until tabs carry a space
id.

The list rules live in SpaceList, which has no Profile or prefs dependency,
and are tested by the new spaces_unittests target. The service is created with
the profile when HeliumSpaces is enabled, and never for incognito, guest or
system profiles. Its prefs are registered by the factory, so the only hook is
registering the factory.

